@@top Feedback Is Infrastructure
:::plain In plain words first
Every trace, failed evaluation, incident and support ticket is a **signal**. The ratchet turns each one into a change at the layer that owns its cause:
- wrong results go to an evaluation or test;
- missing facts go to the context source;
- unsafe actions go to policy;
- timeouts go to runtime controls;
- product questions go to the backlog.

Each change has an owner, a verification and a retirement condition. 14.46 did this for coding-agent corrections; this lesson does it for the product as well. The LLMOps lifecycle is covered in Zero to Agents 12.15 (linked above). This lesson routes the signals the incident-agent story produced in 14.48 to 14.53, closes one loop with a real regression run, and writes the decision brief the practice lab asks for.
